# Credentials for the ACME simulation cloud environment. There are none to
# add: this environment holds no AWS or cluster credentials. Never commit
# real values.

# --- AWS (read-only, via connector) -------------------------------------------
# Claude reads AWS through AWS's managed MCP server, added in claude.ai as a
# custom connector (https://aws-mcp.eu-west-1.api.aws/mcp) and signed in as a
# read-only IAM Identity Center user with the ClaudeReadOnly permission set
# (acme-sim iac/bootstrap/README.md). No access key, network secret or env
# var is involved, so the aws CLI and terraform here run offline only
# (fmt, validate).

# --- Kubernetes --------------------------------------------------------------
# kubectl access to the cluster stays with humans. kubectl and helm here are
# for rendering and linting manifests (kustomize, helm template).

# --- Not needed --------------------------------------------------------------
#   GitHub: the GitHub proxy authenticates git and the GitHub tools with the
#     Claude GitHub App. Leave GH_TOKEN / GITHUB_TOKEN unset.
#   Honeycomb, Slack: use claude.ai connectors (Honeycomb's EU MCP server is
#     https://mcp.eu1.honeycomb.io/mcp, added as a custom connector).
